# Web-UI redesign — implementation evidence (2026-07-19)
# Spec: apps/web-ui/design/ (source of truth). Stack: React 19 + Tailwind v4
# + shadcn-style CVA components, Vite build embedded via RustEmbed (ADR 0004).

== Review standard (brief §7), point by point ==

1. Screens & flows: all 6 screens (G-1 topbar, G-2 sheet, R-1 list, R-2
   composer, R-3 timeline, R-4 result, S-1 config) built with empty/loading/
   error/read-only states. Verified live in Chrome (snapshots + screenshots
   web-ui-*.png).
2. Enter contract: plain Enter & Cmd/Ctrl+Enter submit, Shift+Enter newline,
   isComposing IME guard; Enter submits ONLY in the composer (Composer.tsx
   onKeyDown; global chords in lib/shortcuts.ts).
3. WS bucketing: 12-step run + parallel 5-step run — each timeline showed ONLY
   its own steps (zero leakage; lib/events.ts buckets by run_id, orders by
   seq). Kernel rejection visible on the axis ("proposed action 'rm_rf_slash'
   is not in the action space · retry"). Auto-scroll pauses on manual
   scroll-up with a "↓ New steps" pill (Timeline.tsx pinned-state machine).
4. a11y: Lighthouse Accessibility = 100 (web-ui-lighthouse.json; the 2
   non-a11y fails are 401 console noise from the tokenless audit navigation +
   meta-description, fixed). design/08 fixes present: skip-link first
   focusable, mandatory focus-ring offset, milestone-throttled role=log
   announcements, targets >=24px, glyph+text+color everywhere.
5. Endpoints (curl, ui-demo server):
     GET  /api/v1/runs/{id}/events  no bearer -> 401; with bearer -> 200,
          39 ordered journal entries (note, decision, intent, receipt ... terminal)
     POST /api/v1/runs/{id}/cancel  no bearer -> 401; terminal run -> returned
          unchanged; live "hang" run -> status=canceled, error="canceled from
          the UI" (UI Stop -> inline confirm -> Canceled result verified live)
   History: after a fresh page load, selecting the 12-step run rebuilt the
   full 13-step axis from the replay (D-1). Contract tests: api_test.rs
   run_events_replays_the_full_ordered_journal + cancel_stops_a_live_run.
6. Topologies: 501/read-only (ui-demo, no controller) -> disabled form +
   "fixed at deploy time" banner (web-ui-settings-readonly-501.png); 200/
   editable (real daemon + llama.cpp) -> model chip, prefilled form, real
   Test "✓ Reachable — 200 .../health", SSRF refusal in UI ("✕ Refused —
   ... allowlist"), real run on qwen2.5-0.5b completed (web-ui-daemon-real-
   run.png). Token via fragment (launcher contract unchanged); bare-browser
   sheet works. Reconnection: killed server -> banner "your runs are safe on
   the kernel" + pill disconnected + rows preserved; restart -> auto-
   reconnected (backoff). Narrow (<720px): list/detail stack with back nav.
   smoke-config-ux.sh (daemon path): PASS - no regression.
7. Bundle: dist/ = 300KB total (index.js 259KB raw / 80.5KB gzip, css 26.7KB)
   - ~8x under the 2-2.5MB budget. cargo test --workspace: 142 passed
   (33 suites, incl. 2 new endpoint tests + updated serves_embedded_ui);
   desktop tests 2 passed (incl. standalone_config end-to-end vs the new
   embed); cargo tauri build -> Kelter.app (exit 0); clippy -D warnings clean;
   fmt clean.
8. Stale-dist: dist/ gitignored; CI builds web-ui (pnpm) before cargo in
   check+desktop jobs; Dockerfile gained a node:22 webui stage; a binary
   built without dist serves an explicit "web-ui not built" message instead
   of a silent 404 (static_asset).

