== Deviations from the spec (for Eryk) ==

1. D-1 replay carries NO rejected-proposals/rationale for historical runs:
   the kernel journals decisions/receipts/terminal only (journal.rs) - the
   brief itself scopes D-1 to "czyta istniejacy journal, zadnego nowego
   storage". Live runs show rejections (WS); history shows the executed
   decisions. Full parity would need new journal writes (kernel change) -
   escalation-listed, not done. UI states this honestly.
2. Capability signalling (design/06 §1a "define with the backend"): done via
   response status (404/405 flips cancelSupported/replaySupported for the
   session, hiding the affordance) instead of a new /capabilities endpoint -
   the brief allows exactly two additive endpoints.
3. Cancel emits no WS event (kernel unchanged): the canceling client updates
   from the POST response; other clients see Canceled on their next list
   refresh. Documented, not hidden.

